  "wikipediaSummary": {
    "title": "Avalon (Roxy Music album)",
    "description": "1982 studio album by Roxy Music",
    "extract": "Avalon is the eighth and final studio album by the English rock band Roxy Music, released on 28 May 1982 by E.G. Records and Polydor. It was recorded between 1981 and 1982 at Compass Point Studios in Nassau, Bahamas, and is regarded as the culmination of the smoother, more adult-oriented sound of the band's later work. It has been credited with pioneering the sophisti-pop genre.",
